var documenterSearchIndex = {"docs":
[{"category":"section","location":"reference/developer_guidelines/#Developer-Guidelines","page":"Developer Guidelines","text":"In order to contribute to PowerSystemCaseBuilder.jl repository please read the following sections of InfrastructureSystems.jl and SiennaTemplate.jl documentation in detail:\n\nStyle Guide\nDocumentation Best Practices\nContributing Guidelines\n\nPull requests are always welcome to fix bugs or add additional modeling capabilities.\n\nAll the code contributions need to include tests with a minimum coverage of 70%","title":"Developer Guidelines"},{"category":"section","location":"how_to_guides/add_a_system/#Add-a-System-to-the-Catalog","page":"Add a System to the Catalog","text":"This page guides developers in how to add new PowerSystems.Systems to the PowerSystemCaseBuilder.jl SystemCatalog. If you are a user rather than a developer, please refer to how to Select and Load a Power System instead.","title":"Add a System to the Catalog"},{"category":"section","location":"how_to_guides/add_a_system/#Defining-System-Data-and-Adding-It-To-The-Catalog","page":"Add a System to the Catalog","text":"Adding a new PowerSystems.System to PowerSystemCaseBuilder.jl requires coordinated changes to two repositories: the system is defined and described through custom functions in PowerSystemCaseBuilder.jl, while the underlying data is hosted in the PowerSystemsTestData repository.\n\nThe steps to complete these changes are:\n\nCreate a new folder in the PowerSystemsTestData repository and add the System's input data files, such as .csv, .raw, .dyr, .m, and/or .jl files\nDefine a custom build_* function that loads or compiles your System in the appropriate file in PowerSystemCaseBuilder.jl's src/library/ directory. The files are organized according to SystemCategory. See the existing files in src/library/ for examples.\nDefine a new SystemDescriptor in src/system_descriptor_data.jl, with:\nThe build_function argument pointing to your new build_* function\nThe raw_data argument pointing to either the directory you added in PowerSystemsTestData, or a .jl, .raw, or .m file within it. See the existing systems for examples.","title":"Defining System Data and Adding It To The Catalog"},{"category":"section","location":"how_to_guides/add_a_system/#Testing-the-New-System-Locally","page":"Add a System to the Catalog","text":"Before opening pull requests for both PowerSystemCaseBuilder.jl and PowerSystemsTestData, ensure that your new System builds correctly by testing it locally:\n\nChange the DATA_DIR definition in PowerSystemCaseBuilder.jl's src/definitions.jl to point to your local fork/clone of PowerSystemsTestData\nIn a new Julia REPL, Pkg.develop PowerSystemCaseBuilder.jl, pointing to your local fork/clone\nTry using build_system on your new System and check for errors and accuracy\nFinally, revert changes to the DATA_DIR definition before submitting pull requests","title":"Testing the New System Locally"},{"category":"section","location":"reference/internal/#Internal-API","page":"Internals","text":"","title":"Internal API"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.KNOWN_STALE_SCALING_FACTOR_MULTIPLIERS","page":"Internals","text":"Confirmed stale scaling_factor_multiplier names: a getter that exists in PSY but not on the component type the pointer row applies it to.\n\n\"get_storage_target\" (PowerSystemsTestData-5.0-dev4 5-Bus dataset, 5busts/7day/*.json): a real PSY getter, but only on EnergyReservoirStorage — every occurrence in these pointer files names a HydroReservoir (`HydroReservoir1head,HydroReservoir2head), whose equivalent end-of-simulation target field isleveltargets, i.e.getleveltargets`.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.KNOWN_STALE_SCALING_FACTOR_MULTIPLIERS"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.KNOWN_STALE_TIME_SERIES_ROWS","page":"Internals","text":"Confirmed dangling time-series pointer rows: the referenced component genuinely does not exist anywhere in that dataset's own csv tables.\n\nRTS-GMLC-0.2.3 (rts artifact, RTSSIIPDIR/timeseriespointers.json): 201HYDRO4 is a run-of-river unit (gen.csv: Unit Type = ROR) and, unlike every other *HYDRO* unit, has no storage.csv row — by design it has no HydroReservoir — yet the pointer file still names \"201HYDRO4RESERVOIRhead\" for its inflow/storagetarget series.\n\nPowerSystemsTestData-5.0-dev4 5-Bus dataset (CaseData artifact, 5bus_ts/7day/*.json): the pointer files were evidently authored against a richer template (real solar/wind generators, 4 reserves) than this snapshot's gen.csv (no renewables) / reserves.csv (REG1 only) actually contains.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.KNOWN_STALE_TIME_SERIES_ROWS"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.KNOWN_UNREAD_MATPOWER_SECTIONS","page":"Internals","text":"Matpower fixture data that no Sienna type represents, and that PowerFlowFileParser's OpenAPI builder therefore rejects rather than skips. Matched exactly so any new data of either kind still errors.\n\nne_branch (case3tnep.m, case5tnep.m): PowerModels' transmission-expansion candidate branches.\n\n313_STORAGE_1 (RTS_GMLC.m, gen row 158): a storage unit listed as a generator. Matpower storage belongs in its own storage table, which this case does not have.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.KNOWN_UNREAD_MATPOWER_SECTIONS"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.RTS_USER_DESCRIPTOR_FILE","page":"Internals","text":"Column-to-field map for the RTS-GMLC tables, shipped here rather than read from the RTS artifact.\n\nThe artifact's own user_descriptors.yaml declares neither the emission columns, the MTTF/MTTR and outage-rate columns, the bus shunt columns, the LTE/STE emergency ratings, nor lat/lng — so PowerTableDataParser's emissions, outage, and geographic parsers found nothing, skipped, and that data reached the System nowhere. It survived only as unmapped extras on the document, which PowerSystems does not read back.\n\nThis copy (from PowerTableDataParser.jl/test/descriptors/rts_user_descriptors.yaml, the descriptor its own acceptance tests use) declares them, so the parsers build the attributes the tables describe.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.RTS_USER_DESCRIPTOR_FILE"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder._ZIP_BUCKETS","page":"Internals","text":"The three ways a StandardLoad can hold power: constant power, constant current, and constant impedance.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder._ZIP_BUCKETS"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder._ZIP_QUANTITIES","page":"Internals","text":"The (prefix, suffix) around a bucket name spelling StandardLoad's four power fields per bucket — constant_active_power, max_constant_active_power, and the reactive pair.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder._ZIP_QUANTITIES"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.SystemArgument","page":"Internals","text":"An argument to pass to a SystemDescriptor's build_function\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.SystemArgument"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.SystemArgument-Tuple{}","page":"Internals","text":"SystemArgument(; name, default, allowed_values)\n\n\nReturns an argument to pass to a SystemDescriptor's build_function \n\nExample\n\nSystemArgument(;\n                name = :add_forecasts,\n                default = true,\n                allowed_values = Set([true, false]),\n            )\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.SystemArgument"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystems.System-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractDict}","page":"Internals","text":"System(\n    file_path::AbstractString,\n    md::AbstractDict;\n    solved_case,\n    kwargs...\n) -> PowerSystems.System\n\n\nConstruct a System from a .raw file and a dictionary corresponding to the <name>_export_metadata.json file\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystems.System"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/internal/#Downloads.download","page":"Internals","text":"download(\n    repo::AbstractString,\n    branch::AbstractString,\n    folder::AbstractString\n) -> String\ndownload(\n    repo::AbstractString,\n    branch::AbstractString,\n    folder::AbstractString,\n    force::Bool\n) -> String\n\n\nDownload Data from a \"branch\" into a \"data\" folder in given argument path. Skip the actual download if the folder already exists and force=false. Returns the downloaded folder name.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Downloads.download"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder._consolidate_zip_model!-Tuple{PowerSystems.StandardLoad, Symbol}","page":"Internals","text":"_consolidate_zip_model!(\n    load::PowerSystems.StandardLoad,\n    bucket::Symbol\n)\n\n\nSum a StandardLoad's three ZIP buckets into bucket, zeroing the other two.\n\nSums rather than moves one bucket: a parsed load can already split its power across the three, and selecting a model means the whole load behaves that way. Read and written in device base, the basis the struct stores, so nothing is rescaled.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder._consolidate_zip_model!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder._convert_argument_types!-Tuple{AbstractString, Vector}","page":"Internals","text":"_convert_argument_types!(\n    str::AbstractString,\n    struct_args::Vector\n) -> Any\n\n\nConvert specific parameters to types that are not Float64 for specific inverter components\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder._convert_argument_types!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder._convert_argument_types_for_gen!-Tuple{AbstractString, Vector}","page":"Internals","text":"_convert_argument_types_for_gen!(\n    str::AbstractString,\n    struct_args::Vector\n)\n\n\nConvert specific parameters to types that are not Float64 for specific generator components\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder._convert_argument_types_for_gen!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder._detach_id!-Tuple{Any}","page":"Internals","text":"_detach_id!(component) -> Union{Nothing, Int64}\n\n\nClear a detached component's id so the system it is added to next mints a fresh one.\n\n_duplicate_system moves components out of a deepcopy into the original, where their ids would collide with the very components they were copied from. Reassigning inside the twin first (IS.assign_new_id!) is not enough: the two systems' id counters start out equal, so the twin hands out exactly the ids main_sys is itself handing out to the arcs and lines built along the way. Clearing the id instead lets add_component! draw it from the receiving system — the only counter that can guarantee uniqueness there.\n\nSafe only on a component already removed from its old system, and only because _duplicate_system clears the twin's time series up front: an id is what the time series store and the attribute associations key on.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder._detach_id!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder._instantiate_param_vector_size-Tuple{AbstractString, Dict}","page":"Internals","text":"_instantiate_param_vector_size(\n    str::AbstractString,\n    param_map::Dict\n) -> Any\n\n\nConstruct appropiate vector size for components that collect parameters from more than 2 PSS/E components\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder._instantiate_param_vector_size"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder._is_losslessly_serializable-Tuple{PowerSystems.System, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"_is_losslessly_serializable(\n    sys::PowerSystems.System,\n    name::AbstractString\n) -> Bool\n\n\nWhether sys can round-trip through an OpenAPI document without loss.\n\nForecasts round-trip as of PSY converter-plan §4 (Deterministic, DeterministicSingleTimeSeries, SingleTimeSeries — Probabilistic/Scenarios still do not, see PSY's _missing_structural_field, but no PSCB builder produces either), so that clause is gone. What remains: any component whose type PSY's document converters do not cover at all — dynamics today — per PSY's own is_document_exportable trait (src/openapi/ledger.jl, generated from DOCUMENT_PLAN). Caching such a system anyway would silently truncate it on the next load (a dynamics-carrying system reads back with none — the exact trap this function exists to prevent).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder._is_losslessly_serializable"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder._make_shaft-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Internals","text":"_make_shaft(param_map, val) -> Any\n\n\nCreate a SingleMass shaft struct directly using the parameter mapping.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder._make_shaft"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder._parse_dera1!-Tuple{Any, Any, Any, Dict, Int64}","page":"Internals","text":"_parse_dera1!(\n    bus_dict,\n    componentID,\n    componentValues,\n    param_map::Dict,\n    bus_num::Int64\n)\n\n\nParse dictionary of data (from _parse_dyr_file) into a dictionary of DERA1. The function receives the parsed dictionary and constructs a dictionary indexed by bus, that contains a dictionary with each DERA1 indexed by its id.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder._parse_dera1!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder._parse_dyr_components-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"_parse_dyr_components(\n    dyr_file::AbstractString\n) -> Dict{Int64, Any}\n\n\nParse a .dyr file directly from its name by constructing its dictionary of dictionaries.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder._parse_dyr_components"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder._parse_dyr_components-Tuple{Dict}","page":"Internals","text":"_parse_dyr_components(data::Dict) -> Dict{Int64, Any}\n\n\nParse dictionary of dictionaries of data (from _parse_dyr_file) into a dictionary of struct components. The function receives the parsed dictionary and constructs a dictionary indexed by bus, that contains a dictionary with each dynamic generator and dynamic inverter components (indexed via its id).\n\nFor Generators, each dictionary indexed by id contains a vector with 5 of its components:\n\nMachine\nShaft\nAVR\nTurbineGov\nPSS\n\nFor Inverters, each dictionary indexed by id contains a vector with 7 of its components:\n\nConverter\nActivePowerControl\nReactivePowerControl\nInnerControl\nDCSource\nFrequencyEstimator\nFilter\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder._parse_dyr_components"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder._parse_dyr_file-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"_parse_dyr_file(file::AbstractString) -> Dict{Int64, Dict}\n\n\nParse .dyr file into a dictionary indexed by bus number. Each bus number key has a dictionary indexed by component type and id.\n\nComments in .dyr files are not supported (beginning of lines with //).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder._parse_dyr_file"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder._parse_dyr_generator_components!-Tuple{Dict, Any, Any, Dict, Dict}","page":"Internals","text":"_parse_dyr_generator_components!(\n    bus_dict::Dict,\n    componentID,\n    componentValues,\n    gen_map::Dict,\n    param_map::Dict\n)\n\n\nParse dictionary of data (from _parse_dyr_file) into a dictionary of struct components. The function receives the parsed dictionary and constructs a dictionary indexed by bus, that contains a dictionary with each dynamic generator indexed by its id.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder._parse_dyr_generator_components!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder._parse_dyr_inverter_components!-Tuple{Dict, Dict, Tuple{String, String}, Dict}","page":"Internals","text":"_parse_dyr_inverter_components!(\n    bus_dict::Dict,\n    inv_dict::Dict,\n    componentID::Tuple{String, String},\n    inv_map::Dict\n)\n\n\nParse dictionary of data (from _parse_dyr_file) into a dictionary of struct components. The function receives the parsed dictionary and constructs a dictionary indexed by bus, that contains a dictionary with each dynamic inverter indexed by its id.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder._parse_dyr_inverter_components!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder._populate_args-Tuple{Vector, Any}","page":"Internals","text":"_populate_args(param_map::Vector, val) -> Vector{Any}\n\n\nPopulate arguments in a vector for each dynamic component (except Shafts). Returns a vector with the parameter values of the argument of each component.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder._populate_args"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder._set_zip_load_model!-Tuple{PowerSystems.System, Symbol}","page":"Internals","text":"_set_zip_load_model!(\n    sys::PowerSystems.System,\n    bucket::Symbol\n)\n\n\nGive every load in sys a single ZIP model: :constant, :current or :impedance.\n\nStands in for PSY.set_model!(load, PSY.LoadModels.X). PSY removed the LoadModels enum in its load refactor: the model is now structural — which of StandardLoad's constant_*, current_* and impedance_* pairs carries the power — rather than a tag on the load.\n\nNote this operates on StandardLoad, which is what the PSS/E parser emits; the PowerLoad pass is for systems built some other way, and goes through PSY.convert_component! so the load keeps its id, time series and service memberships.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder._set_zip_load_model!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder._total_zip_power-Tuple{PowerSystems.StandardLoad, AbstractString, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"_total_zip_power(\n    load::PowerSystems.StandardLoad,\n    prefix::AbstractString,\n    suffix::AbstractString\n) -> Any\n\n\nTotal of a StandardLoad's three ZIP buckets for one power quantity, in device base.\n\nprefix is \"\" for the operating point or \"max_\" for the limit, suffix is \"active_power\" or \"reactive_power\" — the halves _ZIP_QUANTITIES pairs up. PSY supplies this aggregate only for max_active_power (get_max_active_power(::StandardLoad, units)), so the other three are summed the same way here.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder._total_zip_power"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder._with_timeseries_metadata_file-Tuple{PowerTableDataParser.PowerSystemTableData, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"_with_timeseries_metadata_file(\n    rawsys::PowerTableDataParser.PowerSystemTableData,\n    path::AbstractString\n) -> PowerTableDataParser.PowerSystemTableData\n\n\nCopy rawsys with timeseries_metadata_file replaced.\n\nField values are taken by name rather than positionally: PowerSystemTableData belongs to PowerTableDataParser, and two of its seven fields are adjacent Dicts, so a reorder there would leave a positional rebuild compiling and silently wrong.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder._with_timeseries_metadata_file"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.add_dyn_injectors!-Tuple{PowerSystems.System, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"add_dyn_injectors!(\n    sys::PowerSystems.System,\n    dyr_file::AbstractString\n)\n\n\nAdd to a system already created the dynamic components. The system should already be parsed from a .raw file.\n\nExamples:\n\ndyr_file = \"Example.dyr\"\nadd_dyn_injectors!(sys, dyr_file)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.add_dyn_injectors!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.build_pwl_average_cost_test_sys-Tuple{}","page":"Internals","text":"build_pwl_average_cost_test_sys(\n;\n    kwargs...\n) -> PowerSystems.System\n\n\nSame as buildpwlincrementalcosttest_sys but converts on the fly to PiecewiseAverageCurve\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.build_pwl_average_cost_test_sys"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.build_pwl_average_fuel_test_sys-Tuple{}","page":"Internals","text":"build_pwl_average_fuel_test_sys(\n;\n    kwargs...\n) -> PowerSystems.System\n\n\nSame as buildpwlincrementalfueltest_sys but converts on the fly to PiecewiseAverageCurve\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.build_pwl_average_fuel_test_sys"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.clear_all_serialized_systems-Tuple{String}","page":"Internals","text":"clear_all_serialized_systems(path::String)\n\n\nDelete all data and files for PowerSystems.Systems that have been serialized\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.clear_all_serialized_systems"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.clear_serialized_system","page":"Internals","text":"clear_serialized_system(name::String)\nclear_serialized_system(\n    name::String,\n    case_args::Dict{Symbol}\n)\n\n\nDelete all files and references associated with a PowerSystems.System that has been serialized\n\nUseful while debugging adding a new System to PowerSystemCaseBuilder.jl to ensure all data and references are removed and that the new build is clean\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.clear_serialized_system"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.deserialize_reverse_component_ids-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{Any, Any, T}} where T<:Type{Int64}","page":"Internals","text":"deserialize_reverse_component_ids(\n    mapping,\n    bus_number_mapping,\n    _::Type{Int64}\n) -> Dict\n\n\nConvert a sbusnsname => pname dictionary to a (pbusn, pname) => s_name dictionary\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.deserialize_reverse_component_ids"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.filter_descriptor_kwargs-Tuple{SystemDescriptor}","page":"Internals","text":"filter_descriptor_kwargs(\n    descriptor::SystemDescriptor;\n    kwargs...\n) -> Dict{Symbol, Any}\n\n\nReturn the keyword arguments passed by the user that apply to the descriptor. Add any default values for fields not passed by the user.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.filter_descriptor_kwargs"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.fix_known_stale_time_series_data-Tuple{PowerTableDataParser.PowerSystemTableData}","page":"Internals","text":"fix_known_stale_time_series_data(\n    rawsys::PowerTableDataParser.PowerSystemTableData\n) -> PowerTableDataParser.PowerSystemTableData\n\n\nReturn rawsys unchanged if it carries no time-series pointer file, or its timeseries_metadata_file matches nothing in KNOWN_STALE_TIME_SERIES_ROWS or KNOWN_STALE_SCALING_FACTOR_MULTIPLIERS. Otherwise return a copy pointing at a fixed temp copy of the pointer file: known-dangling rows dropped, known-stale multiplier names remapped.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.fix_known_stale_time_series_data"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.get_serialized_filepath","page":"Internals","text":"get_serialized_filepath(name::String) -> String\nget_serialized_filepath(\n    name::String,\n    case_args::Dict{Symbol}\n) -> String\n\n\nThe .sns archive holding one cached System, written by PSY.to_file and read by PSY.from_file. The archive is the lossless form: it keeps subsystems, which the document forms drop.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.get_serialized_filepath"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.get_total_system_count-Tuple{SystemCatalog}","page":"Internals","text":"get_total_system_count(sys::SystemCatalog) -> Int64\n\n\nReturns the total number of systems in a SystemCatalog\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.get_total_system_count"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.is_serialized","page":"Internals","text":"is_serialized(name::String) -> Bool\nis_serialized(name::String, case_args::Dict{Symbol}) -> Bool\n\n\nWhether name has a complete cache entry.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.is_serialized"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.name_formatter_from_component_ids-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Internals","text":"name_formatter_from_component_ids(\n    raw_name_mapping,\n    bus_number_mapping,\n    sig\n) -> PowerSystemCaseBuilder.var\"#component_id_formatter#name_formatter_from_component_ids##0\"{Dict{K, V}} where {K, V}\n\n\nUse PSS/E exporter metadata to build a function that maps component names back to their original Sienna values.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.name_formatter_from_component_ids"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.parse_export_metadata_dict-Tuple{AbstractDict}","page":"Internals","text":"parse_export_metadata_dict(\n    md::AbstractDict\n) -> Tuple{Dict, Any}\n\n\nParse an export_metadata dictionary, returning the kwargs that should be passed to the System constructor and the bus number remapping that should be used to effect the retransformation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.parse_export_metadata_dict"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.per_unit_of-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"per_unit_of(\n    quantity_kind::AbstractString\n) -> NamedTuple{(:unit_system, :units, :quantity_kind), <:Tuple{InfrastructureSystems.RelativeUnits.ComponentBaseUnit, Nothing, AbstractString}}\n\n\nKeyword arguments declaring a time series stored per unit on its owner's own base.\n\nReplaces scaling_factor_multiplier, which InfrastructureSystems removed. A normalized profile used to be stored bare next to the name of an accessor, and every read multiplied it by that accessor's value on the owner. The profile is still stored the same way — one shared array many components can point at — but the storage now declares what it is: unit_system says the values are per unit on the component's own base, and quantity_kind names the physical quantity they scale to. That carries the same meaning without a function name for the reader to resolve, and leaves the scaling to the consumer.\n\nunits stays nothing: a per-unit basis is not a units label.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.per_unit_of"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.rate_to_probability-Tuple{Float64, Int64}","page":"Internals","text":"rate_to_probability(\n    for_gen::Float64,\n    mttr::Int64\n) -> @NamedTuple{λ::Float64, μ::Float64}\n\n\nrate_to_probability(for_gen::Float64, mttr::Int64)\n\nConverts the forced outage rate and mean time to repair to the λ and μ parameters\n\nArguments\n\nfor_gen::Float64: Forced outage rate [1/T]\nmttr::Int64: Mean time to repair [T]\n\nReturns\n\nλ::Float64: Transition probability from online to offline [1/T]\nμ::Float64: Transition rate from offline to online [1/T]\n\nReference\n\nhttps://core.ac.uk/download/pdf/13643059.pdf from https://github.com/Sienna-Platform/SiennaPRASInterface.jl/blob/main/src/util/draws/drawhelperfunctions.jl\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.rate_to_probability"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.reservoir_level_quantity-Tuple{PowerSystems.EnergyReservoirStorage}","page":"Internals","text":"reservoir_level_quantity(\n    _::PowerSystems.EnergyReservoirStorage\n) -> String\n\n\nAn EnergyReservoirStorage has no level_data_type to choose from: its storage_capacity is canonically MWh, with conversion_factor scaling a non-MWh medium into it. So its levels are energy however the medium is measured.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.reservoir_level_quantity"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.reservoir_level_quantity-Tuple{PowerSystems.HydroReservoir}","page":"Internals","text":"reservoir_level_quantity(\n    reservoir::PowerSystems.HydroReservoir\n) -> String\n\n\nThe quantity a profile normalized against a reservoir's storage capacity scales to.\n\nDepends on the reservoir: level_data_type decides whether its levels are accounted in energy, in volume, or as a head. PowerTableDataParser owns the mapping so the fixtures and the table parser cannot drift apart on what a reservoir-normalized series means.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.reservoir_level_quantity"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.serialize_case_parameters-Tuple{Dict{Symbol}}","page":"Internals","text":"serialize_case_parameters(case_args::Dict{Symbol})\n\n\nCreates a JSON file informing the user about the meaning of the hash value in the file path if it doesn't exist already\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.serialize_case_parameters"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.serialize_system","page":"Internals","text":"serialize_system(sys::PowerSystems.System, name::String)\nserialize_system(\n    sys::PowerSystems.System,\n    name::String,\n    case_args::Dict{Symbol}\n)\n\n\nWrite sys to the cache entry for name.\n\nThe archive is written under a temporary name and renamed into place, so an interrupted write never leaves a partial archive that is_serialized would report as complete, and concurrent builders of the same system never read each other's half-written file.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.serialize_system"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.sorted_components-Tuple","page":"Internals","text":"sorted_components(args...) -> Any\n\n\nComponents of sys sorted by name. The builders pair positional time-series arrays with components by index, and get_components iterates a Dict, whose order changes between Julia versions.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.sorted_components"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.system_from_document-Tuple{Any}","page":"Internals","text":"system_from_document(oapi; kwargs...) -> PowerSystems.System\n\n\nLoad a parser's OpenAPI document into a System, via a temporary bundle on disk.\n\nTwo reasons the bundle is not skippable today. A document carrying time series has nowhere to hand them over in memory: from_openapi takes a time_series_storage_path and adopts the store it opens from it (_system_with_sidecar), so accepting an already-open store would be what removes the round trip. And PSY's importer expects the round-tripped shape of some values regardless of time series; see the note on the PSS/E method.\n\nto_json writes the sidecar beside the document and from_file resolves it back off the document, so neither path is spelled out here. The bundle is scoped to the call: the adopted store is a working copy, so a bare mktempdir would just hold a dead original until the process exits.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.system_from_document"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.system_from_openapi-Tuple{PowerFlowFileParser.PowerModelsData}","page":"Internals","text":"system_from_openapi(\n    pm_data::PowerFlowFileParser.PowerModelsData;\n    kwargs...\n) -> PowerSystems.System\n\n\nBuild a System from PSS/E or Matpower data.\n\nGoes through the document on disk even though these formats carry no time series and from_openapi would accept the in-memory document directly. Handing it over in memory errors on an LCC line: _hvdc_loss_curve (PSY import_handwritten.jl) reads a value field off the loss curve's function data, which only exists after a JSON round trip normalizes it — PSY's importer is written against the round-tripped shape. Take the shortcut once that is fixed, not before.\n\nThe document carries no system base, so the case's baseMVA is handed to the importer directly; left out, it would default to 100 MVA.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.system_from_openapi"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.system_from_openapi-Tuple{PowerTableDataParser.PowerSystemTableData}","page":"Internals","text":"system_from_openapi(\n    rawsys::PowerTableDataParser.PowerSystemTableData;\n    time_series_resolution,\n    kwargs...\n) -> PowerSystems.System\n\n\nBuild a System from table data. time_series_resolution keeps only the series at that resolution; the filter is applied to the parser's staged series, before the sidecar is written, because the sidecar's catalog — not the document's association rows — is what PowerSystems reads the series back through.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.system_from_openapi"},{"category":"section","location":"reference/generated_catalog/","page":"Full Catalog of Systems","text":"<!– Generated by docs/make.jl from the system catalog. Do not edit by hand. –>","title":"Full Catalog of Systems"},{"category":"section","location":"reference/generated_catalog/#Full-Catalog-of-Systems","page":"Full Catalog of Systems","text":"MatpowerTestSystems\n\n┌──────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────┐\n│\u001b[1m Name                         \u001b[0m│\u001b[1m Descriptor                        \u001b[0m│\n├──────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────┤\n│ matpower_ACTIVSg10k_sys      │ ACTIVSg10k Test system            │\n│ matpower_ACTIVSg2000_sys     │ MATPOWER ACTIVSg2000 Test system  │\n│ matpower_RTS_GMLC_sys        │ Matpower RTS-GMLC Test system     │\n│ matpower_case14_sys          │ Matpower Test system              │\n│ matpower_case24_sys          │ Matpower Test system              │\n│ matpower_case2_sys           │ Matpower Test system              │\n│ matpower_case30_sys          │ Matpower Test system              │\n│ matpower_case3_tnep_sys      │ Matpower Test system              │\n│ matpower_case5_asym_sys      │ Matpower Test system              │\n│ matpower_case5_dc_sys        │ Matpower Test system              │\n│ matpower_case5_gap_sys       │ Matpower Test system              │\n│ matpower_case5_pwlc_sys      │ Matpower Test system              │\n│ matpower_case5_re_sys        │ Matpower Test system              │\n│ matpower_case5_re_uc_pwl_sys │ Matpower Test system              │\n│ matpower_case5_re_uc_sys     │ Matpower Test system              │\n│ matpower_case5_strg_sys      │ Matpower Test system              │\n│ matpower_case5_sys           │ Matpower Test system              │\n│ matpower_case5_tnep_sys      │ Matpower Test system              │\n│ matpower_case5_transformer   │ Matpower Test system              │\n│ matpower_case6_sys           │ Matpower Test system              │\n│ matpower_case7_tplgy_sys     │ Matpower Test system              │\n│ matpower_cats                │ Matpower California test system   │\n│ matpower_frankenstein_00_sys │ Matpower Frankenstein Test system │\n└──────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────┘\n\nPSIDSystems\n\n┌────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│\u001b[1m Name                       \u001b[0m│\u001b[1m Descriptor                                               \u001b[0m│\n├────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 14 Bus Base Case           │ 14 Bus Dynamic Test System Case                          │\n│ 2 Bus Load Tutorial        │ 2 Bus Base System for load tutorials                     │\n│ 2 Bus Load Tutorial Droop  │ 2 Bus Base System for load tutorials with Droop Inverter │\n│ 2 Bus Load Tutorial GENROU │ 2 Bus Base System for load tutorials with GENROU         │\n│ 3 Bus Inverter Base        │ 3 Bus Base System for tutorials                          │\n│ WECC 9 Bus                 │ WECC 9 Bus System with dynamic gens from Sauer and Pai   │\n│ psid_11bus_andes           │ PSID 11-bus Kundur System compared against Andes         │\n│ psid_4bus_multigen         │ PSID Multiple Generators in Single-Bus Test Case         │\n└────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\nPSIDTestSystems\n\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│\u001b[1m Name                                     \u001b[0m│\u001b[1m Descriptor                                                                           \u001b[0m│\n├──────────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ psid_psse_test_avr                       │ PSID AVR Test Cases for PSSE Validation                                              │\n│ psid_psse_test_constantI_load            │ PSID Constant Current Load Test Case                                                 │\n│ psid_psse_test_constantP_load            │ PSID Constant Power Load Test Case                                                   │\n│ psid_psse_test_exp_load                  │ PSID Exponential Load Test Case                                                      │\n│ psid_psse_test_gen                       │ PSID GEN Test Cases for PSSE Validation                                              │\n│ psid_psse_test_pss                       │ PSID PSS Test Cases for PSSE Validation                                              │\n│ psid_psse_test_tg                        │ PSID TG Test Cases for PSSE Validation                                               │\n│ psid_test_3rd_indmotor                   │ PSID System with 3rd-order Induction Motor Test Case                                 │\n│ psid_test_5th_indmotor                   │ PSID System with 5th-order Induction Motor Test Case                                 │\n│ psid_test_droop_inverter                 │ PSID Two Bus Droop GFM Inverter Test Case                                            │\n│ psid_test_gfoll_inverter                 │ PSID Two Bus Grid Following Inverter Test Case                                       │\n│ psid_test_indmotor                       │ PSID System without Induction Motor Test Case                                        │\n│ psid_test_omib                           │ PSID OMIB Test Case                                                                  │\n│ psid_test_pvs                            │ PSID OMIB with Periodic Variable Source Test Case                                    │\n│ psid_test_threebus_5shaft                │ PSID Three Bus 5-shaft Test Case                                                     │\n│ psid_test_threebus_anderson              │ PSID Three Bus Anderson-Fouad Test Case                                              │\n│ psid_test_threebus_genrou_avr            │ PSID Three Bus GENROU with PSAT AVRs Test Case                                       │\n│ psid_test_threebus_machine_vsm           │ PSID Three Bus One-d-One-q Machine against VSM Inverter Test Case                    │\n│ psid_test_threebus_machine_vsm_dynlines  │ PSID Three Bus One-d-One-q Machine against VSM Inverter Test Case with Dynamic Lines │\n│ psid_test_threebus_marconato             │ PSID Three Bus Simple Marconato Test Case                                            │\n│ psid_test_threebus_multimachine          │ PSID Three Bus Multi-Machine Test Case                                               │\n│ psid_test_threebus_multimachine_dynlines │ PSID Three Bus Multi-Machine with Dynamic Lines Test Case                            │\n│ psid_test_threebus_oneDoneQ              │ PSID Three Bus One-d-One-q Test Case                                                 │\n│ psid_test_threebus_psat_avrs             │ PSID Three Bus TG Type I and AVR Type II Test Case                                   │\n│ psid_test_threebus_simple_anderson       │ PSID Three Bus Simple Anderson-Fouad Test Case                                       │\n│ psid_test_threebus_simple_marconato      │ PSID Three Bus Simple Marconato Test Case                                            │\n│ psid_test_threebus_vsm_reference         │ PSID Three Bus Inverter Reference Test Case                                          │\n│ psid_test_vsm_inverter                   │ PSID Two Bus D'Arco VSM Inverter Test Case                                           │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\nPSISystems\n\n┌─────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│\u001b[1m Name                                \u001b[0m│\u001b[1m Descriptor                                                                                                                            \u001b[0m│\n├─────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 2Area 5 Bus System                  │ PSI test system with two areas connected with an HVDC Line                                                                            │\n│ 5_bus_hydro_ed_sys                  │ 5-Bus hydro economic dispatch data                                                                                                    │\n│ 5_bus_hydro_ed_sys_with_targets     │ 5-Bus hydro economic dispatch data with energy targets                                                                                │\n│ 5_bus_hydro_uc_sys                  │ 5-Bus hydro unit commitment data                                                                                                      │\n│ 5_bus_hydro_uc_sys_with_targets     │ 5-Bus hydro unit commitment data with energy targets                                                                                  │\n│ 5_bus_hydro_wk_sys                  │ 5-Bus hydro system for weekly dispatch                                                                                                │\n│ 5_bus_hydro_wk_sys_with_targets     │ 5-Bus hydro system for weekly dispatch with energy targets                                                                            │\n│ 5_bus_matpower_AGC                  │ matpower 5-Bus system with AGC time series                                                                                            │\n│ 5_bus_matpower_DA                   │ matpower 5-Bus system with DA time series                                                                                             │\n│ 5_bus_matpower_RT                   │ matpower 5-Bus system with RT time series                                                                                             │\n│ AC_TWO_RTO_RTS_1Hr_sys              │ Two Area RTO System Connected via AC with 1-hour resolution                                                                           │\n│ AC_TWO_RTO_RTS_5min_sys             │ Two Area RTO System Connected via AC with 5-min resolution                                                                            │\n│ HVDC_TWO_RTO_RTS_1Hr_sys            │ Two Area RTO System Connected via HVDC with 1-hour resolution                                                                         │\n│ HVDC_TWO_RTO_RTS_5min_sys           │ Two Area RTO System Connected via HVDC with 5-min resolution                                                                          │\n│ MTHVDC_two_RTS_DA_sys_noForecast    │ Two RTS systems connected by two multi-terminal HVDC systems                                                                          │\n│ RTS_GMLC_DA_sys                     │ RTS-GMLC Full system from git repo for day-ahead simulations                                                                          │\n│ RTS_GMLC_DA_sys_noForecast          │ RTS-GMLC Full system from git repo for day-ahead simulations                                                                          │\n│ RTS_GMLC_RT_sys                     │ RTS-GMLC Full system from git repo for day-ahead simulations                                                                          │\n│ RTS_GMLC_RT_sys_noForecast          │ RTS-GMLC Full system from git repo for day-ahead simulations                                                                          │\n│ c_sys5_pjm                          │ 5-Bus system                                                                                                                          │\n│ c_sys5_pjm_rt                       │ 5-Bus system                                                                                                                          │\n│ modified_RTS_GMLC_DA_sys            │ Modified RTS-GMLC Full system for day-ahead simulations\\n            with modifications to reserve definitions to improve feasibility │\n│ modified_RTS_GMLC_DA_sys_noForecast │ Modified RTS-GMLC Full system for day-ahead simulations\\n            with modifications to reserve definitions to improve feasibility │\n│ modified_RTS_GMLC_RT_sys            │ Modified RTS-GMLC Full system for real-time simulations\\n            with modifications to reserve definitions to improve feasibility │\n│ modified_RTS_GMLC_RT_sys_noForecast │ Modified RTS-GMLC Full system for real-time simulations\\n            with modifications to reserve definitions to improve feasibility │\n│ modified_RTS_GMLC_realization_sys   │ Modified RTS-GMLC Full system for real-time simulations\\n            with modifications to reserve definitions to improve feasibility │\n│ sys10_pjm_ac_dc                     │ 10-bus system (duplicate 5-bus PJM) with 4-DC bus system                                                                              │\n│ two_area_pjm_DA                     │ 2 Area 5-Bus system                                                                                                                   │\n└─────────────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\nPSITestSystems\n\n┌────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│\u001b[1m Name                               \u001b[0m│\u001b[1m Descriptor                                                                                                        \u001b[0m│\n├────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ batt_test_case_b_sys               │ test system for Storage Energy Target formulation(case-b)                                                         │\n│ batt_test_case_c_sys               │ test system for Storage Energy Target formulation(case-c)                                                         │\n│ batt_test_case_d_sys               │ test system for Storage Energy Target formulation(case-d)                                                         │\n│ batt_test_case_e_sys               │ test system for Storage Energy Target formulation(case-e)                                                         │\n│ batt_test_case_f_sys               │ test system for Storage Energy Target formulation(case-f)                                                         │\n│ c_duration_test                    │ 1 Bus for duration testing                                                                                        │\n│ c_fixed_market_bid_cost            │ 1 bus system with a Fixed MarketBidCost Model                                                                     │\n│ c_linear_cost_test                 │ 1 Bus linear cost for testing                                                                                     │\n│ c_linear_fuel_test                 │ 1 Bus linear fuel curve testing                                                                                   │\n│ c_linear_fuel_test_ts              │ 1 Bus linear fuel curve testing                                                                                   │\n│ c_market_bid_cost                  │ 1 bus system with MarketBidCost Model                                                                             │\n│ c_non_convex_io_pwl_cost_test      │ 1 Bus PWL sos testing                                                                                             │\n│ c_pwl_average_cost_test            │ 1 bus CostCurve{PiecewiseAverageCurve} testing                                                                    │\n│ c_pwl_average_fuel_test            │ 1 bus FuelCurve{PiecewiseAverageCurve} testing                                                                    │\n│ c_pwl_incremental_cost_test        │ 1 Bus PWL incremental cost curve testing                                                                          │\n│ c_pwl_incremental_fuel_test        │ 1 Bus PWL incremental (marginal) fuel curve testing                                                               │\n│ c_pwl_incremental_fuel_test_ts     │ 1 Bus PWL incremental (marginal) fuel curve testing                                                               │\n│ c_pwl_io_cost_test                 │ 1 Bus PWL I/O cost curve testing                                                                                  │\n│ c_pwl_io_fuel_test                 │ 1 Bus PWL I/O fuel curve testing                                                                                  │\n│ c_pwl_io_fuel_test_ts              │ 1 Bus PWL I/O fuel curve testing                                                                                  │\n│ c_quadratic_cost_test              │ 1 Bus quadratic cost for testing                                                                                  │\n│ c_quadratic_fuel_test              │ 1 Bus quadratic fuel curve testing                                                                                │\n│ c_quadratic_fuel_test_ts           │ 1 Bus quadratic fuel curve testing                                                                                │\n│ c_ramp_test                        │ 1-bus for ramp testing                                                                                            │\n│ c_sys14                            │ 14-bus system                                                                                                     │\n│ c_sys14_dc                         │ 14-bus system with DC line                                                                                        │\n│ c_sys14_hvdc_lcc                   │ 14-bus system with a TwoTerminalLCCLine replacing the bus 2-3 AC line                                             │\n│ c_sys14_hvdc_vsc                   │ 14-bus system with a TwoTerminalVSCLine replacing the bus 2-3 AC line                                             │\n│ c_sys5                             │ 5-Bus system                                                                                                      │\n│ c_sys5_all_components              │ 5-Bus system with 5-Bus system with Renewable Energy, Hydro Energy Reservoir, and both StandardLoad and PowerLoad │\n│ c_sys5_bat                         │ 5-Bus system with Storage Device                                                                                  │\n│ c_sys5_bat_ems                     │ 5-Bus system with Storage Device with EMS                                                                         │\n│ c_sys5_dc                          │ Systems with HVDC data in the branches                                                                            │\n│ c_sys5_ed                          │ 5-Bus System for Economic Dispatch Simulations                                                                    │\n│ c_sys5_events                      │ 5-Bus system for testing events                                                                                   │\n│ c_sys5_events_rt                   │ 5-Bus system for testing events with real time data                                                               │\n│ c_sys5_hy                          │ 5-Bus system with HydroDispatch                                                                                   │\n│ c_sys5_hy_cascading_turbine_energy │ 5-Bus system with Cascading HydroTurbines with Energy Reservoirs                                                  │\n│ c_sys5_hy_cascading_turbine_head   │ 5-Bus system with HydroTurbine with Reservoir using Head (in meters) data                                         │\n│ c_sys5_hy_ed                       │ 5-Bus system with Hydro-Power for Economic Dispatch Simulations                                                   │\n│ c_sys5_hy_ems_ed                   │ 5-Bus system with Hydro-Power for Economic Dispatch Simulations                                                   │\n│ c_sys5_hy_ems_uc                   │ 5-Bus system with Hydro-Power for Unit Commitment Simulations                                                     │\n│ c_sys5_hy_turbine_energy           │ 5-Bus system with HydroTurbine with Energy Reservoir                                                              │\n│ c_sys5_hy_turbine_head             │ 5-Bus system with HydroTurbine with Reservoir using Head (in meters) data                                         │\n│ c_sys5_hy_uc                       │ 5-Bus system with Hydro-Power for Unit Commitment Simulations                                                     │\n│ c_sys5_hybrid                      │ 5-Bus system with Hybrid devices                                                                                  │\n│ c_sys5_hybrid_ed                   │ 5-Bus system with Hybrid devices and thermal devices for ED.                                                      │\n│ c_sys5_hybrid_uc                   │ 5-Bus system with Hybrid devices and thermal UC devices                                                           │\n│ c_sys5_hyd                         │ 5-Bus system with Hydro Energy Reservoir                                                                          │\n│ c_sys5_hyd_ems                     │ 5-Bus system with Hydro Energy Reservoir                                                                          │\n│ c_sys5_hydro_pump_energy           │ 5-Bus system with hydro pump storage                                                                              │\n│ c_sys5_il                          │ System with Interruptible Load                                                                                    │\n│ c_sys5_ml                          │ Test System with Monitored Line                                                                                   │\n│ c_sys5_pglib                       │ 5-Bus with ThermalMultiStart                                                                                      │\n│ c_sys5_pglib_sim                   │ 5-Bus with ThermalMultiStart for simulation                                                                       │\n│ c_sys5_phes_ed                     │ 5-Bus system with Hydro Pumped Energy Storage for Economic Dispatch Simulations                                   │\n│ c_sys5_pwl_ed                      │ 5-Bus with pwl cost function                                                                                      │\n│ c_sys5_pwl_ed_nonconvex            │ 5-Bus with SOS cost function for Economic Dispatch Simulations                                                    │\n│ c_sys5_pwl_uc                      │ 5-Bus with SOS cost function for Unit Commitment Simulations                                                      │\n│ c_sys5_radial                      │ 5-Bus with a radial branches                                                                                      │\n│ c_sys5_re                          │ 5-Bus system with Renewable Energy                                                                                │\n│ c_sys5_re_fuel_cost                │ 5-Bus system with Renewable Energy and Fuel Cost TimeSeries                                                       │\n│ c_sys5_re_only                     │ 5-Bus system with only Renewable Energy                                                                           │\n│ c_sys5_uc                          │ 5-Bus system for Unit Commitment Simulations                                                                      │\n│ c_sys5_uc_non_spin                 │ 5-Bus system for Unit Commitment with Non-Spinning Reserve Simulations                                            │\n│ c_sys5_uc_re                       │ 5-Bus system for Unit Commitment Simulations with Renewable Units                                                 │\n│ case10_radial_series_reductions    │ Test system for radial and series reductions                                                                      │\n│ case11_network_reductions          │ Test system for building simulations with network reductions                                                      │\n│ hydro_test_case_b_sys              │ test system for HydroGen Energy Target formulation(case-b)                                                        │\n│ hydro_test_case_c_sys              │ test system for HydroGen Energy Target formulation(case-c)                                                        │\n│ hydro_test_case_d_sys              │ test system for HydroGen Energy Target formulation(case-d)                                                        │\n│ hydro_test_case_e_sys              │ test system for HydroGen Energy Target formulation(case-e)                                                        │\n│ hydro_test_case_f_sys              │ test system for HydroGen  Energy Target formulation(case-f)                                                       │\n│ test_RTS_GMLC_sys                  │ RTS-GMLC test system with day-ahead forecast                                                                      │\n│ test_RTS_GMLC_sys_with_hybrid      │ RTS-GMLC test system with day-ahead forecast and HybridSystem                                                     │\n└────────────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\nPSSEParsingTestSystems\n\n┌────────────────────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│\u001b[1m Name                                       \u001b[0m│\u001b[1m Descriptor                                                                                                                                           \u001b[0m│\n├────────────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Base_Eastern_Interconnect_515GW            │ Synthetic Eastern Interconnection system with 515 GW of generation                                                                                   │\n│ PSSE 30 Test System                        │ PSSE 30 Test system                                                                                                                                  │\n│ isolated_bus_test_system                   │ PSSE isolated bus test system                                                                                                                        │\n│ psse_14_network_reduction_test_system      │ PSSE network reduction test system                                                                                                                   │\n│ psse_14_tap_correction_test_system         │ PSSE tap correction test system                                                                                                                      │\n│ psse_14_zero_impedance_branch_test_system  │ PSSE zero impedance branch test system                                                                                                               │\n│ psse_4_zero_impedance_3wt_test_system      │ PSSE zero impedance 3-winding transformer test system                                                                                                │\n│ psse_ACTIVSg2000_sys                       │ PSSE ACTIVSg2000 Test system                                                                                                                         │\n│ psse_RTS_GMLC_sys                          │ PSSE .raw RTS-GMLC system                                                                                                                            │\n│ psse_modified_14bus_nominal_icd            │ Modified 14-bus PSS/E system with 2W and 3W transformers carrying impedance correction tables at nominal tap settings (all correction factors = 1.0) │\n│ psse_modified_14bus_off_nominal_icd        │ Modified 14-bus PSS/E system with transformer tap/angle settings off-nominal, activating impedance correction tables with correction factors ≠ 1.0   │\n│ psse_ybus_14_test_system                   │ PSSE ybus test system                                                                                                                                │\n│ pti_case10_voltage_winding_correction_sys  │ PSSE case10 winding voltage correction test system                                                                                                   │\n│ pti_case11_with_synchronous_condensers_sys │ PSSE Case 11 with Synch. Condensers                                                                                                                  │\n│ pti_case14_sys                             │ PSSE 14-bus Test system                                                                                                                              │\n│ pti_case14_with_interruptible_loads_sys    │ PSSE with interruptible loads Test system                                                                                                            │\n│ pti_case14_with_pst3w_sys                  │ PSSE Case 14 with PST3W                                                                                                                              │\n│ pti_case16_complete_sys                    │ PSSE Case 16 with All Network Components                                                                                                             │\n│ pti_case24_sys                             │ PSSE 24-bus Test system                                                                                                                              │\n│ pti_case30_sys                             │ PSSE 30-bus Test system                                                                                                                              │\n│ pti_case3_sys                              │ PSSE 3-bus Test system                                                                                                                               │\n│ pti_case5_alc_sys                          │ PSSE 5-Bus alc Test system                                                                                                                           │\n│ pti_case5_sys                              │ PSSE 5-Bus Test system                                                                                                                               │\n│ pti_case73_sys                             │ PSSE 73-bus Test system                                                                                                                              │\n│ pti_case7_tplgy_sys                        │ PSSE 7-bus Test system                                                                                                                               │\n│ pti_case8_voltage_winding_correction_sys   │ PSSE case8 winding voltage correction test system                                                                                                    │\n│ pti_frankenstein_00_2_sys                  │ PSSE frankenstein Test system                                                                                                                        │\n│ pti_frankenstein_00_sys                    │ PSSE frankenstein Test system                                                                                                                        │\n│ pti_frankenstein_20_sys                    │ PSSE frankenstein Test system                                                                                                                        │\n│ pti_frankenstein_70_sys                    │ PSSE frankenstein Test system                                                                                                                        │\n│ pti_modified_case14_sys                    │ PSSE Modified 14-bus Test system                                                                                                                     │\n│ pti_modified_case25_v35_sys                │ PSSE Modified 25-bus V35 Test system                                                                                                                 │\n│ pti_parser_test_a_sys                      │ PSSE Test system                                                                                                                                     │\n│ pti_three_winding_mag_test_sys             │ PSSE Test system                                                                                                                                     │\n│ pti_three_winding_test_2_sys               │ PSSE Test system                                                                                                                                     │\n│ pti_three_winding_test_sys                 │ PSSE Test system                                                                                                                                     │\n│ pti_two_terminal_hvdc_test_sys             │ PSSE Test system                                                                                                                                     │\n│ pti_two_winding_mag_test_sys               │ PSSE Test system                                                                                                                                     │\n│ pti_vsc_hvdc_test_sys                      │ PSSE Test system                                                                                                                                     │\n└────────────────────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\nPSYTestSystems\n\n┌─────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│\u001b[1m Name                            \u001b[0m│\u001b[1m Descriptor                                                      \u001b[0m│\n├─────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ dynamic_inverter_sys            │ PSY test dynamic inverter system                                │\n│ psse_240_parsing_sys            │ Test parsing of PSSE 240 Bus Case system                        │\n│ psse_3bus_SEXS_sys              │ Test parsing of PSSE 3-bus Test system with SEXS                │\n│ psse_3bus_gen_cls_sys           │ Test parsing of PSSE 3-bus Test system with CLS                 │\n│ psse_3bus_no_cls_sys            │ Test parsing of PSSE 3-bus Test system without CLS              │\n│ psse_Benchmark_4ger_33_2015_sys │ Test parsing of PSSE Benchmark system                           │\n│ psse_OMIB_sys                   │ Test parsing of PSSE OMIB Test system                           │\n│ psse_renewable_parsing_1        │ Test parsing PSSE 3-bus Test system with REPCA, REECB and REGCA │\n│ tamu_ACTIVSg2000_sys            │ TAMU ACTIVSg2000 Test system                                    │\n└─────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\nSPISystems\n\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│\u001b[1m Name                                        \u001b[0m│\u001b[1m Descriptor                                                                                                              \u001b[0m│\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ RTS_GMLC_5min with Static Outage Data       │ 5 minute RTS_GMLC System with Static GeometricDistributionForcedOutage SupplementalAttribute                            │\n│ RTS_GMLC_5min with TimeSeries Outage Data   │ 5 minute RTS_GMLC System with GeometricDistributionForcedOutage SupplementalAttribute and Outage Probability TimeSeries │\n│ RTS_GMLC_Hourly with Static Outage Data     │ Hourly RTS_GMLC System with Static GeometricDistributionForcedOutage SupplementalAttribute                              │\n│ RTS_GMLC_Hourly with TimeSeries Outage Data │ Hourly RTS_GMLC System with GeometricDistributionForcedOutage SupplementalAttribute and Outage Probability TimeSeries   │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘","title":"Full Catalog of Systems"},{"category":"section","location":"how_to_guides/explore_load/#Select-and-Load-a-Power-System","page":"Select and Load a Power System","text":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.jl offers a catalog of power system test data, already formatted and available to load as PowerSystems.System objects.","title":"Select and Load a Power System"},{"category":"section","location":"how_to_guides/explore_load/#Select","page":"Select and Load a Power System","text":"View the available categories of power systems in the catalog using show_categories:\n\nshow_categories()\nMatpowerTestSystems\nPSIDSystems\nPSIDTestSystems\nPSISystems\nPSITestSystems\nPSSEParsingTestSystems\nPSYTestSystems\nSPISystems\n\nChoose a category, or explore the SystemCategory documentation to learn about each category.\n\nUse show_systems to see the name and description of the available PowerSystems.Systems in the selected category, e.g, PSISystems:\n\nshow_systems(PSISystems)\n┌─────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│\u001b[1m Name                                \u001b[0m│\u001b[1m Descriptor                                                                                                                            \u001b[0m│\n├─────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 2Area 5 Bus System                  │ PSI test system with two areas connected with an HVDC Line                                                                            │\n│ 5_bus_hydro_ed_sys                  │ 5-Bus hydro economic dispatch data                                                                                                    │\n│ 5_bus_hydro_ed_sys_with_targets     │ 5-Bus hydro economic dispatch data with energy targets                                                                                │\n│ 5_bus_hydro_uc_sys                  │ 5-Bus hydro unit commitment data                                                                                                      │\n│ 5_bus_hydro_uc_sys_with_targets     │ 5-Bus hydro unit commitment data with energy targets                                                                                  │\n│ 5_bus_hydro_wk_sys                  │ 5-Bus hydro system for weekly dispatch                                                                                                │\n│ 5_bus_hydro_wk_sys_with_targets     │ 5-Bus hydro system for weekly dispatch with energy targets                                                                            │\n│ 5_bus_matpower_AGC                  │ matpower 5-Bus system with AGC time series                                                                                            │\n│ 5_bus_matpower_DA                   │ matpower 5-Bus system with DA time series                                                                                             │\n│ 5_bus_matpower_RT                   │ matpower 5-Bus system with RT time series                                                                                             │\n│ AC_TWO_RTO_RTS_1Hr_sys              │ Two Area RTO System Connected via AC with 1-hour resolution                                                                           │\n│ AC_TWO_RTO_RTS_5min_sys             │ Two Area RTO System Connected via AC with 5-min resolution                                                                            │\n│ HVDC_TWO_RTO_RTS_1Hr_sys            │ Two Area RTO System Connected via HVDC with 1-hour resolution                                                                         │\n│ HVDC_TWO_RTO_RTS_5min_sys           │ Two Area RTO System Connected via HVDC with 5-min resolution                                                                          │\n│ MTHVDC_two_RTS_DA_sys_noForecast    │ Two RTS systems connected by two multi-terminal HVDC systems                                                                          │\n│ RTS_GMLC_DA_sys                     │ RTS-GMLC Full system from git repo for day-ahead simulations                                                                          │\n│ RTS_GMLC_DA_sys_noForecast          │ RTS-GMLC Full system from git repo for day-ahead simulations                                                                          │\n│ RTS_GMLC_RT_sys                     │ RTS-GMLC Full system from git repo for day-ahead simulations                                                                          │\n│ RTS_GMLC_RT_sys_noForecast          │ RTS-GMLC Full system from git repo for day-ahead simulations                                                                          │\n│ c_sys5_pjm                          │ 5-Bus system                                                                                                                          │\n│ c_sys5_pjm_rt                       │ 5-Bus system                                                                                                                          │\n│ modified_RTS_GMLC_DA_sys            │ Modified RTS-GMLC Full system for day-ahead simulations\\n            with modifications to reserve definitions to improve feasibility │\n│ modified_RTS_GMLC_DA_sys_noForecast │ Modified RTS-GMLC Full system for day-ahead simulations\\n            with modifications to reserve definitions to improve feasibility │\n│ modified_RTS_GMLC_RT_sys            │ Modified RTS-GMLC Full system for real-time simulations\\n            with modifications to reserve definitions to improve feasibility │\n│ modified_RTS_GMLC_RT_sys_noForecast │ Modified RTS-GMLC Full system for real-time simulations\\n            with modifications to reserve definitions to improve feasibility │\n│ modified_RTS_GMLC_realization_sys   │ Modified RTS-GMLC Full system for real-time simulations\\n            with modifications to reserve definitions to improve feasibility │\n│ sys10_pjm_ac_dc                     │ 10-bus system (duplicate 5-bus PJM) with 4-DC bus system                                                                              │\n│ two_area_pjm_DA                     │ 2 Area 5-Bus system                                                                                                                   │\n└─────────────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘","title":"Select"},{"category":"section","location":"how_to_guides/explore_load/#Build","page":"Select and Load a Power System","text":"Finally, use build_system to load your selected system:\n\nsys = build_system(PSISystems, \"5_bus_hydro_ed_sys\")\n\u001b[1m          System\u001b[0m\n┌────────────────┬───────┐\n│\u001b[1m Property       \u001b[0m│\u001b[1m Value \u001b[0m│\n├────────────────┼───────┤\n│ Name           │       │\n│ Description    │       │\n│ Base Power     │ 100.0 │\n│ Base Frequency │ 60.0  │\n│ Num Components │ 36    │\n└────────────────┴───────┘\n\n\u001b[1m                Static Components\u001b[0m\n┌───────────────────────────────────────┬───────┐\n│\u001b[1m Type                                  \u001b[0m│\u001b[1m Count \u001b[0m│\n├───────────────────────────────────────┼───────┤\n│ ACBus                                 │ 5     │\n│ Arc                                   │ 6     │\n│ Area                                  │ 2     │\n│ HydroDispatch                         │ 1     │\n│ HydroReservoir                        │ 2     │\n│ HydroTurbine                          │ 2     │\n│ Line                                  │ 5     │\n│ LoadZone                              │ 2     │\n│ OnlineReserve{ReserveUp, NaturalUnit} │ 1     │\n│ PowerLoad                             │ 3     │\n│ ThermalStandard                       │ 5     │\n│ TwoWindingTransformer                 │ 2     │\n└───────────────────────────────────────┴───────┘\n\n\u001b[1m                            StaticTimeSeries Summary\u001b[0m\n┌────────────────┬──────────────────────────┬──────────────────┬────────────────\n│\u001b[1m owner_type     \u001b[0m│\u001b[1m owner_category           \u001b[0m│\u001b[1m name             \u001b[0m│\u001b[1m time_series_t\u001b[0m ⋯\n│\u001b[90m String         \u001b[0m│\u001b[90m InfraStore.OwnerCategory \u001b[0m│\u001b[90m String           \u001b[0m│\u001b[90m String       \u001b[0m ⋯\n├────────────────┼──────────────────────────┼──────────────────┼────────────────\n│ HydroDispatch  │ Component                │ max_active_power │ SingleTimeSer ⋯\n│ HydroReservoir │ Component                │ inflow           │ SingleTimeSer ⋯\n│ HydroReservoir │ Component                │ storage_target   │ SingleTimeSer ⋯\n│ HydroTurbine   │ Component                │ hydro_budget     │ SingleTimeSer ⋯\n│ HydroTurbine   │ Component                │ max_active_power │ SingleTimeSer ⋯\n│ PowerLoad      │ Component                │ max_active_power │ SingleTimeSer ⋯\n└────────────────┴──────────────────────────┴──────────────────┴────────────────\n\u001b[36m                                                               5 columns omitted\u001b[0m\n\u001b[1m                                Forecast Summary\u001b[0m\n┌────────────────┬──────────────────────────┬──────────────────┬────────────────\n│\u001b[1m owner_type     \u001b[0m│\u001b[1m owner_category           \u001b[0m│\u001b[1m name             \u001b[0m│\u001b[1m time_series_t\u001b[0m ⋯\n│\u001b[90m String         \u001b[0m│\u001b[90m InfraStore.OwnerCategory \u001b[0m│\u001b[90m String           \u001b[0m│\u001b[90m String       \u001b[0m ⋯\n├────────────────┼──────────────────────────┼──────────────────┼────────────────\n│ HydroDispatch  │ Component                │ max_active_power │ Deterministic ⋯\n│ HydroReservoir │ Component                │ inflow           │ Deterministic ⋯\n│ HydroReservoir │ Component                │ storage_target   │ Deterministic ⋯\n│ HydroTurbine   │ Component                │ hydro_budget     │ Deterministic ⋯\n│ HydroTurbine   │ Component                │ max_active_power │ Deterministic ⋯\n│ PowerLoad      │ Component                │ max_active_power │ Deterministic ⋯\n└────────────────┴──────────────────────────┴──────────────────┴────────────────\n\u001b[36m                                                               7 columns omitted\u001b[0m\n","title":"Build"},{"category":"section","location":"how_to_guides/explore_load/#Next-Steps","page":"Select and Load a Power System","text":"Refer to the PowerSystems.jl documentation for how to modify the test system or build your own, and the PowerSimulations.jl and PowerSimulationsDynamics.jl documentation for how to set up and run simulations.","title":"Next Steps"},{"category":"section","location":"reference/public/#Public-API-Reference","page":"Public API","text":"","title":"Public API Reference"},{"category":"section","location":"reference/public/#System-Catalog","page":"Public API","text":"","title":"System Catalog"},{"category":"section","location":"reference/public/#Reading-the-Catalog","page":"Public API","text":"","title":"Reading the Catalog"},{"category":"section","location":"reference/public/#Categories-of-Systems","page":"Public API","text":"","title":"Categories of Systems"},{"category":"section","location":"reference/public/#Building-a-System","page":"Public API","text":"","title":"Building a System"},{"category":"section","location":"reference/public/#Utilities","page":"Public API","text":"","title":"Utilities"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.SystemCatalog","page":"Public API","text":"A container for a catalog of PowerSystems.System data sets\n\nExample\n\nSystemCatalog()\n\nReturns the PowerSystemCaseBuilder.jl catalog\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.SystemCatalog"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.list_categories-Tuple{}","page":"Public API","text":"list_categories() -> Vector{DataType}\n\n\nReturns a vector of SystemCategorys available in the PowerSystemCaseBuilder.jl SystemCatalog\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.list_categories"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.list_systems-Tuple{Type{<:SystemCategory}}","page":"Public API","text":"list_systems(\n    category::Type{<:SystemCategory}\n) -> Vector{String}\n\n\nReturns a vector of names of the systems available in one SystemCategory in the PowerSystemCaseBuilder.jl SystemCatalog\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.list_systems"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.show_categories-Tuple{}","page":"Public API","text":"show_categories()\n\n\nPrints the names of the SystemCategorys available in the PowerSystemCaseBuilder.jl catalog\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.show_categories"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.show_systems-Tuple{Type{<:SystemCategory}}","page":"Public API","text":"show_systems(\n    category::Type{<:SystemCategory};\n    kwargs...\n) -> Any\n\n\nPrints the name and description of all PowerSystems.Systems in a selected SystemCategory in the PowerSystemCaseBuilder.jl catalog\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.show_systems"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.show_systems-Tuple{}","page":"Public API","text":"show_systems(; kwargs...)\n\n\nPrints the name and description of all PowerSystems.Systems in the PowerSystemCaseBuilder.jl catalog, grouped by SystemCategory\n\nSee also: show_systems for a selected category\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.show_systems"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.SystemCategory","page":"Public API","text":"Supertype of categories that group test PowerSystems.Systems for similar use     cases\n\nCurrent subtypes with example Systems for running test simulations include:\n\nPSISystems\nPSIDSystems\n\nSubtypes for testing other packages include:\n\nPSYTestSystems\nPSSEParsingTestSystems\nMatpowerTestSystems\nPSITestSystems\nPSIDTestSystems\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.SystemCategory"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.MatpowerTestSystems","page":"Public API","text":"Category of PowerSystems.Systems to test parsing Matpower files.\n\nSystems only include data for the power flow case.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.MatpowerTestSystems"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.PSIDSystems","page":"Public API","text":"Category of example PowerSystems.Systems for running     PowerSimulationsDynamics.jl     simulations.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.PSIDSystems"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.PSIDTestSystems","page":"Public API","text":"Category of PowerSystems.Systems for PowerSimulationsDynamics.jl package testing.\n\nwarning: Warning\nNot all Systems are functional.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.PSIDTestSystems"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.PSISystems","page":"Public API","text":"Category of example PowerSystems.Systems for running     PowerSimulations.jl     operations problems and simulations.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.PSISystems"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.PSITestSystems","page":"Public API","text":"Category of PowerSystems.Systems for PowerSimulations.jl package testing.\n\nwarning: Warning\nNot all Systems are functional.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.PSITestSystems"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.PSSEParsingTestSystems","page":"Public API","text":"Category of PowerSystems.Systems to test parsing PSSe .raw files. \n\nSystems only include data for the power flow case.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.PSSEParsingTestSystems"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.PSYTestSystems","page":"Public API","text":"Category of PowerSystems.Systems for PowerSystems.jl package testing.\n\nwarning: Warning\nNot all Systems are functional.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.PSYTestSystems"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.SPISystems","page":"Public API","text":"Category for SiennaPRASInterface.jl examples.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.SPISystems"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/public/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.build_system","page":"Public API","text":"build_system(\n    category::Type{<:SystemCategory},\n    name::String;\n    ...\n) -> Any\nbuild_system(\n    category::Type{<:SystemCategory},\n    name::String,\n    print_stat::Bool;\n    force_build,\n    assign_new_uuids,\n    skip_serialization,\n    system_catalog,\n    kwargs...\n) -> Any\n\n\nBuilds a PowerSystems.System from one of the predefined categories of test systems\n\nArguments\n\ncategory::Type{<:SystemCategory}: A subtype of SystemCategory\nname::String: Name of the System to build\n\nAccepted Key Words\n\nprint_stat::Bool = false: Print statistics about the system build process\nforce_build::Bool: true runs entire build process, false (Default) uses deserializiation if possible\nassign_new_uuids::Bool: Retained for signature compatibility and effectively always  true. A cached System is read from an OpenAPI document, which carries component ids  rather than UUIDs, so every load rebuilds components with fresh UUIDs and there is nothing  to reassign. Passing false warns, since stable UUIDs across loads can no longer be  delivered.\nskip_serialization::Bool: Default is false\nsystem_catalog::SystemCatalog: Defaults to the PowerSystemCaseBuilder.jl catalog of Systems\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.build_system"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.SystemDescriptor-Tuple{}","page":"Public API","text":"SystemDescriptor(\n;\n    name,\n    description,\n    category,\n    build_function,\n    raw_data,\n    download_function,\n    stats,\n    supported_arguments\n)\n\n\nConstructs a container for describing, categorizing, and building a PowerSystems.System\n\nArguments\n\nname::AbstractString: Unique name of the System\ndescription::AbstractString: Phrase describing the System and key distinguishing features from other systems in the catalog\ncategory::Type{<:SystemCategory}: A subtype of SystemCategory for categorizing this System within the catalog\nraw_data::AbstractString: A path pointing to the System's data directory, .jl file, or parseable .m or .raw file in PowerSystemsTestData\nbuild_function::Function: A custom Function for building this System. See src/library files.\ndownload_function::Union{Nothing, Function}: Typically unused\nstats::Union{Nothing,SystemBuildStats}: Container for summary statistics on the build process\nsupported_arguments::Vector{SystemArgument}: Additional arguments to pass to the build_function\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.SystemDescriptor"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.SystemBuildStats-Tuple{}","page":"Public API","text":"SystemBuildStats(\n;\n    count,\n    initial_construct_time,\n    serialize_time,\n    min_deserialize_time,\n    max_deserialize_time,\n    total_deserialize_time\n)\n\n\nReturns a container for the summary statistics on the build process for a PowerSystems.System\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.SystemBuildStats"},{"category":"section","location":"#PowerSystemCaseBuilder.jl","page":"Welcome","text":"","title":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#Overview","page":"Welcome","text":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.jl is a Julia package that provides a library of power systems test cases using the PowerSystems.jl data model: PowerSystems.System.\n\nPowerSystemCaseBuilder.jl is a simple tool to build power systems ranging from 5-Bus systems to entire grid systems for the purpose of testing or prototyping power system models. This package facilitates the open sharing of data sets for power systems modeling.\n\nThe main features include:\n\nComprehensive and extensible library of power systems for modeling.\nAutomated serialization/de-serialization of cataloged PowerSystems.Systems.\n\nPowerSystemCaseBuilder.jl is an active project under development, and we welcome your feedback, suggestions, and bug reports.","title":"Overview"},{"category":"section","location":"#About-Sienna","page":"Welcome","text":"PowerSystemCaseBuilder.jl is part of the National Laboratory of the Rockies (formerly known as NREL)'s Sienna ecosystem, an open source framework for power system modeling, simulation, and optimization. The Sienna ecosystem can be found on Github. It contains three applications:\n\nSienna\\Data enables efficient data input, analysis, and transformation\nSienna\\Ops enables enables system scheduling simulations by formulating and solving optimization problems\nSienna\\Dyn enables system transient analysis including small signal stability and full system dynamic simulations\n\nEach application uses multiple packages in the Julia programming language.","title":"About Sienna"},{"category":"section","location":"#Installation-and-Quick-Links","page":"Welcome","text":"Sienna installation page: Instructions to install PowerSystemCaseBuilder.jl and other Sienna\\Data packages\nSienna Documentation Hub: Links to other Sienna packages' documentation","title":"Installation and Quick Links"}]
}
